  "theme": "chalk",
  "question": "The noise rating $N$ decibels and the intensity $I$ are connected by $N = 10\\lg\\dfrac{I}{k}$, where $k$ is a constant. A hot water pump is rated $50$ dB and a dishwasher $62$ dB. Find how many times as intense the dishwasher is as the pump, correct to 3 significant figures.",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "equation-steps",
      "scroll": true,
      "steps": [
        {
          "heading": "Step 1: put in both readings",
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "N=10\\lg\\dfrac{I}{k}", "id": "q0" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "\\text{readings}\\;\\to\\;\\text{subtract}\\;\\to\\;\\text{un-log}", "id": "p1", "hl": "sky" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "62", "id": "n62" },
            { "tex": "=10\\lg\\dfrac{I_d}{k}", "id": "r62" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "50", "id": "n50" },
            { "tex": "=10\\lg\\dfrac{I_p}{k}", "id": "r50" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Step 2: subtract",
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "62-50", "id": "m" },
            { "tex": "=10\\lg\\dfrac{I_d}{k}-10\\lg\\dfrac{I_p}{k}", "id": "rhs" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "12", "id": "f12" },
            { "tex": "=10\\lg\\left(\\dfrac{I_d}{k}\\div\\dfrac{I_p}{k}\\right)", "id": "l5r" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "12", "id": "d12" },
            { "tex": "=10\\lg\\dfrac{I_d}{I_p}", "id": "l6r" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Step 3: un-log",
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "\\lg\\dfrac{I_d}{I_p}=1.2", "id": "l7" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "\\dfrac{I_d}{I_p}=10^{1.2}", "id": "l8" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "tex": "=15.8\\;\\text{(3 s.f.)}", "id": "ans", "hl": "emerald" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "N equals ten log of I over K. The dishwasher is sixty-two decibels, and the pump is fifty.",
          "asks": ["What is a decibel?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 0 }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b1.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b1.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "We want how many times as intense: a ratio. Plan: put in both readings, subtract, then un-log.",
          "asks": ["Why is it a ratio?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "token": "p1", "on": "Plan: put in both readings" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b2.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b2.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "Put in the dishwasher: sixty-two equals ten log of I D over K.",
          "asks": ["What is I D?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 2, "on": "sixty-two equals ten log" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b3.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b3.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "And the pump: fifty equals ten log of I P over K.",
          "asks": ["Why subtract the two?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 3, "on": "fifty equals ten log" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b4.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b4.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "Subtract the two readings, so Minus Power can join the logs. Sixty-two minus fifty equals the difference of the two logs.",
          "asks": ["Why subtract, not divide?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 4, "on": "Sixty-two minus fifty" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b5.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b5.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "Both logs have the same base, ten. Minus Power joins them into one log of a division.",
          "asks": ["What is Minus Power?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "rhs", "on": "Both logs have" },
            {
              "do": "note",
              "text": "Minus Power: $\\lg M - \\lg N = \\lg\\tfrac{M}{N}$",
              "near": "rhs",
              "on": "Minus Power joins them"
            }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b6.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b6.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "So twelve equals ten log of I D over K, divided by I P over K.",
          "asks": ["Where did twelve come from?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 5, "on": "So twelve equals" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b7.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b7.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "The K on top and the K below cancel, so K drops out. Twelve equals ten log of I D over I P.",
          "asks": ["Why does K cancel?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 6, "on": "Twelve equals ten log" }
          ],
          "audio": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b8.mp3",
          "timing": "/lessons/log-scales-am/scene-01-b8.timing.json"
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide both sides by ten. Log of the ratio is one point two.",
          "asks": ["Why divide by ten?"],
          "do": [
